---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import Glossary from "../../components/Glossary.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import HistoryTimeline from "../../components/HistoryTimeline.astro";
import history from "../../data/history.json";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/asbe/asbe21.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "1. Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "2. Scope and Effective Date" },
        { id: "s3", label: "3. The Single On-Balance-Sheet Lessee Model" },
        { id: "s4", label: "4. Initial Measurement" },
        { id: "s5", label: "5. Subsequent Measurement" },
        { id: "s6", label: "6. Exemptions — Short-Term and Low-Value Leases" },
        { id: "s7", label: "7. Lessor Accounting — Dual Classification Retained" },
        { id: "s8", label: "8. Worked Example — Initial Recognition of a Lease" },
        { id: "s9", label: "9. Worked Example — the Short-Term Lease Exemption" },
        { id: "s10", label: "10. Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s11", label: "11. Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates" },
        { id: "s12", label: "12. Relationship to IFRS 16" },
        { id: "s13", label: "13. Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s14", label: "14. Related Standards" },
        { id: "s15", label: "15. Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">
<div class="hub-sub">Extended reference poster · Chinese GAAP (ASBE / CAS) · 租赁 · Revised, IFRS 16-aligned single on-balance-sheet lessee model · RMB examples</div></div></div>



<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Bringing substantially all leases onto the lessee's Balance Sheet</div><div class="principle">ASBE No. 21 was REVISED to introduce a SINGLE on-BALANCE-SHEET LESSEE model — REQUIRING recognition of a "RIGHT-OF-USE ASSET" and a CORRESPONDING lease LIABILITY for SUBSTANTIALLY all leases — CLOSELY mirroring IFRS 16'S own approach internationally, and ELIMINATING the OLDER dual finance/OPERATING lessee CLASSIFICATION model.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope and Effective Date</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">All lessees, with dual classification retained for lessors</div><div class="principle">This Standard applies to ALL companies that are LESSEES (WITH continued dual CLASSIFICATION for lessor ACCOUNTING — Section 7), effective from JANUARY 1, 2021 for ALL enterprises — a REVISION broadly PARALLELING IFRS 16'S own international ROLLOUT, WITH only a MODEST delay relative to IFRS 16'S 2019 effective date.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>The Single On-Balance-Sheet Lessee Model</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">No more off-balance-sheet operating leases</div><div class="text-supporting">UNDER the REVISED Standard, a LESSEE recognises a RIGHT-OF-USE asset and a LEASE liability for VIRTUALLY all leases — ELIMINATING the OLD "operating LEASE" category'S off-balance-SHEET treatment entirely, SUBJECT to the NARROW exemptions in Section 6 — a SINGLE, unified LESSEE accounting MODEL replacing the PREVIOUS dual finance/OPERATING classification.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Initial Measurement</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Present value of lease payments, plus adjustments</div><div class="text-supporting">The LEASE liability is INITIALLY measured at the PRESENT value of REMAINING lease PAYMENTS, discounted USING the rate IMPLICIT in the LEASE (or, WHERE not readily DETERMINABLE, the LESSEE'S incremental BORROWING rate). The RIGHT-OF-USE asset is INITIALLY measured at COST — GENERALLY the initial LEASE liability, PLUS any LEASE payments MADE at or BEFORE commencement, INITIAL direct COSTS, and ESTIMATED restoration COSTS.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Subsequent Measurement</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Depreciation of the asset, interest accretion on the liability</div><div class="text-supporting">The RIGHT-OF-USE asset is DEPRECIATED (GENERALLY straight-LINE) over the SHORTER of the LEASE term or the ASSET'S useful LIFE. The LEASE liability is REDUCED as PAYMENTS are MADE, with INTEREST expense ACCRETING the liability OVER time.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Exemptions — Short-Term and Low-Value Leases</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Narrow relief, mirroring IFRS 16's own exceptions</div><div class="text-supporting">A LESSEE MAY elect NOT to APPLY the on-BALANCE-SHEET model to SHORT-TERM leases (GENERALLY 12 MONTHS or LESS, with NO purchase OPTION) or LEASES of LOW-VALUE underlying ASSETS — recognising LEASE payments as an EXPENSE on a STRAIGHT-LINE basis INSTEAD, CONSISTENT with IFRS 16's OWN narrow exemptions.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Lessor Accounting — Dual Classification Retained</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Finance vs operating classification continues for lessors</div><div class="text-supporting">UNLIKE the LESSEE-side reform, LESSOR accounting CONTINUES to DISTINGUISH between FINANCE leases (SUBSTANTIALLY transferring the RISKS and REWARDS of OWNERSHIP, derecognising the UNDERLYING asset and recognising a LEASE receivable) and OPERATING leases (RETAINING the underlying ASSET on the LESSOR'S own Balance SHEET, recognising LEASE income on a STRAIGHT-LINE basis) — CONSISTENT with IFRS 16'S own RETENTION of dual LESSOR classification internationally.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Worked Example — Initial Recognition of a Lease</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Recognising the right-of-use asset and lease liability</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A 5-year warehouse lease</div><div class="wk-body">A company enters a 5-year warehouse lease with annual payments of RMB 15,000,000, discounted using an incremental borrowing rate of 4%, giving a present value of lease payments of approximately RMB 66,800,000.</div><div class="wk-answer">The company recognises a RIGHT-OF-USE ASSET and a LEASE LIABILITY of approximately <strong>RMB 66,800,000</strong> EACH at commencement — REPLACING what WOULD previously have been a SIMPLE straight-LINE rental EXPENSE under the OLD operating lease TREATMENT.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example — the Short-Term Lease Exemption</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Retaining off-balance-sheet treatment for a genuinely short lease</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A 9-month equipment rental</div><div class="wk-body">A company rents equipment for a 9-month project, with no purchase option or expectation of renewal, at RMB 1,500,000 per month.</div><div class="wk-answer">The company ELECTS the SHORT-TERM lease EXEMPTION, recognising RMB 1,500,000 of RENTAL expense EACH month on a STRAIGHT-line basis — WITHOUT recognising a RIGHT-of-use ASSET or LEASE liability.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASBE No. 21 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Right-of-use assets and lease liabilities, by class of underlying asset</span><span>Maturity analysis of lease liabilities</span><span>Information about short-term/low-value lease exemptions elected</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Determining the lease term, including renewal/termination options reasonably certain to be exercised</span><span>Classifying a lessor arrangement as finance or operating</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Incremental borrowing rate where the rate implicit in the lease is not readily determinable</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Relationship to IFRS 16</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — ASBE 21 vs IFRS 16</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASBE 21</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IFRS 16</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Lessee model</span><span>Single on-balance-sheet model</span><span>Single on-balance-sheet model — converged</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Lessor classification</span><span>Dual finance/operating retained</span><span>Dual finance/operating retained — converged</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">A GENUINELY thoroughly CONVERGED reform — CHINA'S adoption of the ON-balance-sheet lessee MODEL came only MODESTLY later than IFRS 16'S own INTERNATIONAL effective DATE, a CONTRAST to Japan GAAP'S considerably LONGER lag on the SAME topic.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every lease event lands</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Lease commencement</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span></span><span>Right-of-use asset and lease liability recognised</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Depreciation and interest</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bp">IS</span></span><span>Depreciation on the asset, interest accretion on the liability</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASBE No. 17</span><span>Borrowing Costs — relevant for the interest expense treatment on lease liabilities</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Right-of-use asset</div><div class="glossary-def">The asset recognised by a lessee representing its right to use a leased asset over the lease term.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Incremental borrowing rate</div><div class="glossary-def">The rate a lessee would have to pay to borrow funds to obtain an asset of similar value, used when the rate implicit in the lease is not readily determinable.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Chinese GAAP / ASBE terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><div class="litem"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (资产负债表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bp">IS</span> Income Statement (利润表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bo">SCOE</span> Statement of Changes in Owners' Equity (所有者权益变动表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bc">CFS</span> Cash Flow Statement (现金流量表)</div></div></div>


</div>
  </div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.asbe21 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
